The pizza slice is a rectangle of roughly 130 px by 200 px. Converting to cm, that is about 8 cm by 12 cm, though it is tilted, so the true length is probably closer to 11 cm. A thin-crust rectangular slice of that size is about 1 cm thick. The volume is roughly 8 × 11 × 1 = 88 cm³. Pizza is fairly dense but airy, so I'll use about 0.8 g/cm³, which gives roughly 70 g. Cheese pizza at 270 kcal/100 g is a reasonable value. I'll estimate the slice at about 75 g.

